  "You drop the last four feet to the ground.",
  "A cold gust of wind swirls snow into your face, making it difficult to see clearly, but you press on through the forest.",
  "Given the rate at which the searchlights are turning, it would be suicidal to attempt anything other than a direct run at the tower to the north.",
  "You walk around the house to the back; the door is closed.",
  "You reenter the forest and soon come to a roadway running from east to west.",
  "You walk around the house and into the clearing.",
  "You stumble through a three-foot snowdrift, but get back on your feet quickly and move to a point in the forest at which a small road leads south.",
